WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
In 1983, American psychologist, Howard Gardner

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.780
published a book [Frames of Mind] with a theory

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.840
that there are nine types of intelligence:

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.800
To understand this theory,

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.160
let’s consider the problem of the council of Newtown,

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.060
who wants to build a bridge
over the dangerous railroad tracks.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:24.460
But there is strong opposition from some citizens
who don't like change.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.320
Despite the demonstrations,

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.340
the council agrees to go ahead

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.699
and then hires a team of 9 experts

00:00:30.699 --> 00:00:33.520
from Smarts &amp; Co. to get the job done.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.780
Let’s introduce each one of them:

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.600
Miss Picture Smart played a lot of hide and
seek when she was young.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.480
And she loved puzzles.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.240
She has lots of imagination and ideas about shapes.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.180
Her job in the project is to create the plans,

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.180
make the designs and build a prototype.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.080
Mr. Nature Smart loves trees

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.240
and he has great ideas of how to minimize the impact

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.480
of a bridge on the environment.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.440
He started thinking of these issues

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.040
ever since the first time he went 
summer camping with dad.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.400
He developed a passion for all living beings.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.560
Mrs. Number Smart is a nerd.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:17.880
She always was.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.700
In the playground, she was already calculating

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.040
the sand buckets needed to build the biggest castle.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.580
In high-school, she was the Chess-master

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.160
and everyone was so proud her.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.920
She will calculate the costs,

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.040
study workers safety issues

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.660
and estimate the raw materials needed.

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:39.960
Her concerns are the budget, resources and risks.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.920
Mrs. People Smart arranges a town meeting

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:46.420
and goes out to invite all the citizens to come.

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:48.640
She was always good with people.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:52.320
As a kid, she spent most of the time outside
with her neighbours.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.760
As a teenager, her mom explained to her that
most people mean well,

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.700
even if they have trouble showing their feelings.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.700
Today, everyone loves her

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.220
and she does a great job convincing everyone,

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:07.620
even the most outspoken opponents.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:14.120
Miss Word Smart has been keeping a diary since she was young.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.500
In math class, she wrote poems

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.340
and during field trips she didn't talk to others but

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:21.940
instead studied the travel guide.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:25.840
For the big town hall meeting, she writes
a convincing speech,

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:30.520
filled with hard facts, big feelings and good metaphors.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:37.080
Ever since he was young, Jimmy Life Smart
knew how to talk and entertain.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:40.050
Today he shows his skills on the stage.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.320
He starts his speech with a personal story

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.860
about his cat that once got lost on the train tracks.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:49.100
Then he delivers all the arguments
with so much passion,

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:52.660
that all citizens can only agree with the plan.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:57.020
Ms. Word Smart is delighted
to see the impact of her work.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:04.120
Now, as construction starts, Mr. Body Smart
gets ready to get things done.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:08.360
Even the children are inspired by his power
and want to help.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:11.400
During the breaks, he plays football with his team,

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.760
which is fun and teaches him balance skills

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.420
he later can use high up in the sky.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.520
Madame Self Smart knows a lot about feelings:

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.440
our fears, joys and angers.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.200
She learned this from her own past

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.700
where she started to reflect on herself.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.060
But she also reads a lot about feelings

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:35.020
and talks to her friends about their emotions.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:38.060
During the construction, she is the positive force,

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:40.180
motivates those that feel down,

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:44.280
and solves tensions that can come up
when we collaborate.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.500
While everyone is busy finishing the bridge,

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:52.340
Mrs. Music Smart writes a song for the grand opening.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:56.400
She has loved music ever since started playing piano.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.860
Later she moved on to Hip Hop and Jazz-Dance.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.880
At the opening ceremony of the bridge,

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.540
she and her band perform the song.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:09.460
It was a fantastic team effort from all 9
of the Smart and Co.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:19.000
In 2016, Gardner said that he is considering
adding pedagogical intelligence, or “teach smart”.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.380
What do you think?

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:22.960
Is he right or wrong about these types,

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:28.640
or are IQ, EQ or other forms of intelligence better classifications?

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:34.800
Please be teach smart, and tell us what you
think about intelligence theory in the comments below.

